## 131. storage/logs/.gitkeep - Logs Git Placeholder

**File Location:** `storage/logs/.gitkeep`

**Purpose:** Ensures logs directory exists in Git repository.

```text
# ============================================================
# Logs Directory - Git Placeholder
# ============================================================
# This file ensures the logs directory is tracked by Git.
# The actual log files are excluded via .gitignore.
# ============================================================

# The logs directory is used by the application to store:
# - Error logs
# - Access logs
# - Activity logs
# - Security logs
# - Audit logs

# This file ensures the directory structure exists
# when cloning the repository.

# Git ignore rules should exclude:
# *.log
# *.log.*
# *.log-*
# *.txt
# *.tmp

# Directory permissions should be:
# - Owner: web server user
# - Group: web server group
# - Permissions: 0750

# Log files should have permissions:
# - Owner: web server user
# - Group: web server group
# - Permissions: 0640

# For more information, see README.md